{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Recommendation Serendipity.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Recommendation Serendipity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"recommendation serendipity recommendation serendipity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Recommendation Serendipity.md","fileName":"Recommendation Serendipity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Recommendation Serendipity","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-10-04 14:56\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Recommender System Evolution]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Recommender System Evolution","Exploration-Exploitation Tradeoff","recommendationengines.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Recommendation Serendipity.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Recommendation Serendipity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"recommendation serendipity recommendation serendipity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Recommendation Serendipity.md","fileName":"Recommendation Serendipity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Recommendation Serendipity","heading":"Recommendation Serendipity","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Recommendation serendipity is an unexpectedly relevant suggestion that helps a user discover an appealing option outside the most predictable continuation of prior behavior. It requires relevance and surprise together: an unfamiliar item that has no value to the user is merely random.\n\nSimilarity provides a credible path from known preferences, while diversity and novelty prevent the candidate set from collapsing into repetition. The [[Exploration-Exploitation Tradeoff]] therefore shapes serendipity: the system must spend some opportunities learning beyond safe recommendations without sacrificing so much relevance that users stop trusting it.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Recommender System Evolution","E